;FOUR COPIES OF THE RECEPTOR IN ASU. TWO PAIRS OF HOMODIMERS OF THE RECEPTOR ARE INVOLVED IN A PROPER DOMAIN SWAP INVOLVING THE N-TERMINAL 527-553 AMINO ACIDS. NO EVIDENCE THAT THIS HOMODIMER IS BIOLOGICALLY RELEVANT. THE INTERACTION FORMED BETWEEN RECEPTOR AND NCOR PEPTIDE IS BIOLOGICALLY RELEVANT.
;
